## Environment Clarification

- **Local (Windows/PowerShell)**: Commands like `docker compose` are run here. `nmcli` will **not** work here.
- **Remote (ZimaOS/Linux)**: You must **SSH** into your ZimaOS machine to run `nmcli`, `nmtui`, or other system commands.

## Passwordless Sudo (ZimaOS)

To stop the system from asking for your password every time you run a `sudo` command on ZimaOS:

1. SSH into the ZimaOS machine.
2. Run this command (it will create a permission file for your current user):
   ```bash
   echo "$USER ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL" | sudo tee /etc/sudoers.d/90-passwordless-sudo
   ```
3. From now on, `sudo` commands will not ask for a password.
